WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.662
So how will we know it's
working, and what do we need?

2
00:00:02.662 --> 00:00:07.951
Five measures, each baselined in phase
one and each one something leadership can

3
00:00:07.951 --> 00:00:13.318
read: hours from separation to blocked
access, orphaned accounts trending to zero,

4
00:00:13.318 --> 00:00:17.659
fewer joiner and mover tickets,
managers and organizations in the

5
00:00:17.659 --> 00:00:22.000
directory matching HR, and every
exception with an owner and an age.

6
00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:27.001
From leadership, we need one decision:
start HR-driven identity now,

7
00:00:27.001 --> 00:00:32.912
as a design requirement of both the HR
2.0 onboarding and the Entra ID migration.

8
00:00:32.912 --> 00:00:36.648
To act on it: a sponsor across
HR, identity and privacy;

9
00:00:36.648 --> 00:00:42.035
identity named as a consumer in the HR
2.0 interconnection plan; data owners

10
00:00:42.035 --> 00:00:44.988
designated and the person key confirmed;

11
00:00:44.988 --> 00:00:48.463
and a small team for the
pre-onboarding data work.

12
00:00:48.463 --> 00:00:52.505
HR-Driven Identity has the full
design, every claim footnoted,

13
00:00:52.505 --> 00:00:57.262
and Identity and Directory covers
the directory migration it builds on.

14
00:00:57.262 --> 00:00:58.080
Thank you.
